  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'a) A scholar and religious person of great reputation, Longchen Rabjam (1306-64) stands out as a prominent visitor to Bhutan among the Tibetan treasure discoverers. Elucidate some of the great works of Longchen Rabjam which subsequently had strong implications for the establishment of the Nyingthig tradition in Bhutan. (10 marks)', 'a) Longchen Rabjam (Longchenpa) was one of the greatest scholars of the Nyingma school. His great works include the Seven Treasuries (Dzod Dun) and his trilogies, which systematised Dzogchen philosophy and the Nyingthig (''heart essence'') teachings. Political conflict in Tibet led him to spend years in exile in Bhutan (around the 1350s), mainly in Bumthang. There he: (1) founded eight monasteries known as the ''eight lings'', such as Tharpaling in Bumthang; (2) taught and wrote extensively, spreading Nyingthig practice; (3) left a family lineage and disciples who continued his teachings. Later, the great Bhutanese terton Pema Lingpa (1450-1521) was regarded as an emanation of Longchenpa, and Pema Lingpa''s lineage spread Nyingthig teachings across central and eastern Bhutan. Longchenpa''s works therefore laid the foundations of the Nyingma Nyingthig tradition that is still practised in Bhutan today.', null, '[{"point": "Longchenpa: great Nyingma master and writer (Seven Treasuries, Trilogies), systematised Dzogchen and the Nyingthig (heart essence) teachings; came to Bhutan in exile (c. 1350s)", "marks": 4}, {"point": "In Bhutan: founded the ''eight lings'' (e.g. Tharpaling in Bumthang); taught and wrote; his lineage and descendants; Pema Lingpa regarded as his emanation, so Nyingthig spread through Pema Lingpa''s line; lasting Nyingma practice in central and eastern Bhutan", "marks": 6}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development') and t.slug = 'history-longchen-rabjam-and-jamgon-ngawang-gyaltshen'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-general-3'), 'standard', 10,
    1080, 'historical_official', 'awaiting_review',
    null, null,
    '{"verdict": "pass", "issues": [], "checker_notes": "Model answer, marking guide and rubric written by Claude from the RCSC paper; facts were checked against what is widely published, but please read before publishing. Real past-paper questions keep RCSC wording.", "batch": "ME Paper III (General): BCSE 2021, batch 2", "source": {"title": "BCSE 2021 Main Examination, General category, Paper III", "year": 2021, "url": "https://rcsc.gov.bt/bcse-past-question-papers/"}}'::jsonb, 'me-general-3-2021b2-a2', 1, null, null, null, null)
  returning id
)
