with nq as (
  insert into public.questions (stage, question_type, stem, model_answer, explanation, key_points, subject_id, topic_id, paper_id, difficulty, marks,
                                estimated_seconds, origin, status, parent_question_id, variation_type, ai_review, passage_group, passage_position, verified_by, subject_group_id, specialisation_id, image_url)
  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'b) Bhutan can take pride in the numerous Drukpa religious masters who have appeared throughout its recorded history. One such master is Jamgon Ngawang Gyaltshen (1647-1732), whose legacy has proved enduring in numerous fields relating to religious arts, crafts and ritual practices, diplomatic role and also institutionally through his family-based incarnation line and monastery. Discuss the most important legacies of Jamgon Ngawang Gyaltshen covering his unique diplomatic role in service to the Bhutanese state, namely that of "monk ambassador". (10 marks)', 'b) Jamgon Ngawang Gyaltshen was an eminent Drukpa master of the period after Zhabdrung. His legacies include: (1) Religious arts and crafts - he is remembered as a patron and master of sacred art, commissioning statues, thangkas and ritual objects, and building or restoring temples; (2) Ritual practices - he developed and transmitted rituals and practices that continued in the monastic tradition; (3) Diplomatic role - as a ''monk ambassador'' he represented the Bhutanese state on missions to Tibet and neighbouring Himalayan rulers, using his religious standing to negotiate peace and good relations when Bhutan was under external pressure; (4) Institutional legacy - his family-based incarnation line (the Jamgon trulkus) and its monastery preserved his teachings and works for generations. His life shows how religious masters served both the Dharma and the security of the young Bhutanese state.', null, '[{"point": "Religious arts, crafts and rituals: commissioning/ making statues, paintings and ritual objects, ritual practices and dances; building and restoring temples", "marks": 4}, {"point": "Diplomatic role as ''monk ambassador'': represented the Bhutanese state in missions to Tibet and neighbouring Himalayan courts, negotiating peace and relations; institutional legacy through his incarnation line (Jamgon trulkus) and monastery", "marks": 6}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development') and t.slug = 'history-longchen-rabjam-and-jamgon-ngawang-gyaltshen'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-general-3'), 'standard', 10,
    1080, 'historical_official', 'awaiting_review',
    null, null,
    '{"verdict": "pass", "issues": [], "checker_notes": "Model answer, marking guide and rubric written by Claude from the RCSC paper; facts were checked against what is widely published, but please read before publishing. Real past-paper questions keep RCSC wording.", "batch": "ME Paper III (General): BCSE 2021, batch 2", "source": {"title": "BCSE 2021 Main Examination, General category, Paper III", "year": 2021, "url": "https://rcsc.gov.bt/bcse-past-question-papers/"}}'::jsonb, 'me-general-3-2021b2-a2', 2, null, null, null, null)
  returning id
