  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'b) His Majesty the King said: "I have seen many people describe democracy as a jewel gifted to the people from the Throne. I would say that rather than a gift, democracy is the responsibility given to the people to further strengthen the country..." In the light of what His Majesty The King explained, discuss some of the duties and responsibilities of Bhutanese citizens that you think would be most important in a democratic society to further strengthen our country. (10 marks)', 'b) His Majesty reminds us that democracy is not only a right but a responsibility. Important duties of citizens (many set out in Article 8 of the Constitution) include: (1) upholding the sovereignty, unity and security of the country and the Constitution; (2) voting wisely and participating in elections and local governance, choosing candidates on merit rather than personal gain; (3) remaining united after elections, showing tolerance and respect for different views and avoiding regional or party divisions; (4) acting with integrity, refusing to give or take bribes, and reporting corruption; (5) obeying laws and paying taxes; (6) protecting the environment and preserving culture and values; (7) serving the community and nation, for example through De-suung and volunteering; and (8) using social media responsibly and sharing accurate information. When citizens fulfil these responsibilities, democracy strengthens the country.', null, '[{"point": "Duties (Article 8): uphold sovereignty, unity and the Constitution; vote responsibly and participate; tolerance, respect and avoiding divisions; integrity and fighting corruption; protecting the environment and culture; paying taxes, obeying laws; service (De-suung, volunteering); accurate information and responsible use of social media", "marks": 10}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development') and t.slug = 'dzongs-and-democracy'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-general-3'), 'standard', 10,
    1080, 'historical_official', 'awaiting_review',
    null, null,
    '{"verdict": "pass", "issues": [], "checker_notes": "Model answer, marking guide and rubric written by Claude from the RCSC paper; facts were checked against what is widely published, but please read before publishing. Real past-paper questions keep RCSC wording.", "batch": "ME Paper III (General): BCSE 2021, batch 2", "source": {"title": "BCSE 2021 Main Examination, General category, Paper III", "year": 2021, "url": "https://rcsc.gov.bt/bcse-past-question-papers/"}}'::jsonb, 'me-general-3-2021b2-a3', 2, null, null, null, null)
