  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'a) A civil servant must be apolitical in service of the Tsa-Wa-Sum as per the Civil Service Values and Conduct. In your opinion, why should civil servants remain apolitical? Discuss some of the significant challenges faced and what you think needs to be done to overcome those challenges. (10 marks)', 'a) Civil servants must be apolitical because they serve every elected government and every citizen impartially. This ensures continuity and stability when governments change, fairness in service delivery regardless of party loyalty, merit-based appointments and promotions, and public trust in the government machinery. The Civil Service Act 2010 and the Bhutan Civil Service Rules require civil servants to stay out of party politics.
Challenges: in a small society, many civil servants have relatives and friends in politics; there is pressure from politicians to show favours; elections can create perceptions that transfers and postings are political; and civil servants may express political views on social media.
What needs to be done: the RCSC should enforce clear rules on political neutrality, protect civil servants from political interference, keep human resource decisions strictly merit-based, provide training on civil service values, issue guidelines on social media use, and senior leaders must set the example.', null, '[{"point": "Why apolitical: serve every elected government impartially, continuity and stability, fairness to all citizens, merit-based system, public trust, protect Tsa-Wa-Sum; Civil Service Act 2010 and BCSR", "marks": 4}, {"point": "Challenges: pressure from politicians and relatives in politics, election-time favours, transfers/ postings perceived as political, social media posts, small society with close family ties", "marks": 3}, {"point": "Solutions: clear rules and enforcement by RCSC, training on values, protection from political interference, merit-based HR, responsible social media guidelines, leadership by example", "marks": 3}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development') and t.slug = 'civil-service-and-the-monarchy'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-general-3'), 'standard', 10,
