  values ('ME', 'long_answer', 'a) Patronage of the arts has been an undertaking of royal families in monarchical cultures. In Bhutan, Her Majesty the Grand Queen Mother, Kesang Choeden Wangchuck, has always involved herself as a patron of important religious figures, monasteries, and rituals. Discuss some of Her Majesty''s significant works which contributed towards improving the religious and socio-cultural life of the people of Bhutan. (10 marks)', 'a) Her Majesty the Grand Queen Mother Ashi Kesang Choeden Wangchuck has been one of the greatest patrons of religion and culture in modern Bhutan. Her contributions include: (1) patronage of great religious masters of both the Nyingma and Drukpa traditions, inviting them to give teachings and empowerments and supporting their activities in Bhutan; (2) sponsoring important rituals and prayers for the wellbeing of the King, the country and its people; (3) building and restoring temples, monasteries and stupas - for example, she built the third temple at Kurjey in Bumthang in 1990; (4) supporting the printing and preservation of sacred texts and religious arts such as statues and thangkas; and (5) supporting monastic communities and the preservation of Bhutan''s cultural heritage. Her patronage has enriched the spiritual life of the people, preserved sacred sites and traditions, and strengthened the place of religion in Bhutanese society.', null, '[{"point": "Patronage of religious masters and lineages (e.g. Nyingma and Drukpa teachers), sponsoring teachings, empowerments and rituals for the nation", "marks": 3}, {"point": "Building and restoring temples, monasteries and stupas (e.g. the third temple at Kurjey, Bumthang, 1990), supporting printing of sacred texts and religious arts; social contributions and preservation of heritage", "marks": 7}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
