  values ('ME', 'analytical', 'The Round Table Meeting (RTM) was initiated in the early 1980s and is the highest forum for policy dialogue between Bhutan and its development partners. The Royal Government accords highest importance to the RTM, and it is being held twice over the course of a Five Year Plan period. The 15th RTM was held on 2nd September 2021.
Discuss the importance of the RTM for Bhutan and its development partners. (20 marks)', 'The Round Table Meeting, started in the early 1980s with UNDP support, brings together the Royal Government and its development partners - bilateral partners such as India, Japan and the EU, UN agencies, the World Bank and the Asian Development Bank - for high-level policy dialogue, usually at the start of a Five Year Plan and at its mid-term review. The 15th RTM was held on 2 September 2021.
Importance for Bhutan:
1. It is a platform to present the Plan''s priorities, progress and challenges to all partners together.
2. It helps mobilise financial and technical resources for the Plan.
3. It aligns partners'' support with national priorities, ensuring Bhutan''s ownership of its development.
4. It improves coordination and avoids duplication among partners.
5. It serves as a mid-term review, allowing course correction.
6. It allows Bhutan to explain emerging issues - for example COVID-19 recovery, graduation from LDC status, youth unemployment and climate change - and seek support.
7. It showcases Bhutan''s GNH approach, good governance and transparency, building partners'' confidence.
Importance for development partners:
1. They understand Bhutan''s policies and priorities directly from the government.
2. It supports aid effectiveness, accountability and results monitoring.
3. Partners coordinate among themselves.
4. It strengthens long-term partnership and trust.
As Bhutan graduates from LDC status and grant aid declines, the RTM becomes even more important for shifting from aid to partnerships in trade, investment, technology and climate finance.', null, '[{"point": "Explains RTM: high-level policy dialogue forum with development partners (UN agencies, multilateral banks, bilateral partners), held around the FYP (start and mid-term reviews)", "marks": 4}, {"point": "Importance for Bhutan: present plan priorities and progress, mobilise resources and technical support, align aid with national priorities, coordination and avoid duplication, mid-term review, share challenges (COVID-19, LDC graduation, unemployment), showcase GNH and transparency", "marks": 9}, {"point": "Importance for partners: understand Bhutan''s priorities and policies, ensure aid effectiveness and accountability, coordinate among partners, monitor results, strengthen partnerships and trust", "marks": 5}, {"point": "Conclusion: shift from aid to partnership as Bhutan graduates", "marks": 2}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'bhutan-institutions-development'),
